          <li class="type-item" data-type="class">
            <button type="button" aria-controls="type-preview" aria-pressed="false">
              <span class="type-no">07</span><span class="type-name"><small class="type-kind" data-i18n="class-k">Class / interface</small><span data-i18n="class-h">Which types fulfil which contracts?</span></span>
            </button>
            <div class="type-detail"><div><p data-i18n="class-p">Classes and interfaces with their members — inheritance, implementation, composition and dependencies, each drawn in its own notation.</p></div></div>
          </li>
          <li class="type-item" data-type="tree">
            <button type="button" aria-controls="type-preview" aria-pressed="false">
              <span class="type-no">08</span><span class="type-name"><small class="type-kind" data-i18n="tree-k">Tree</small><span data-i18n="tree-h">How is it organised?</span></span>
            </button>
            <div class="type-detail"><div><p data-i18n="tree-p">One root and its branches — a repository's modules, a product platform, a team, or a taxonomy, level by level.</p></div></div>
          </li>
          <li class="type-item" data-type="timeline">
            <button type="button" aria-controls="type-preview" aria-pressed="false">
              <span class="type-no">09</span><span class="type-name"><small class="type-kind" data-i18n="timeline-k">Timeline</small><span data-i18n="timeline-h">What happened, and when?</span></span>
            </button>
            <div class="type-detail"><div><p data-i18n="timeline-p">Events on a real time axis — an incident, a release history, a project — with time zones handled and long quiet stretches broken out.</p></div></div>
          </li>
          <li class="type-item" data-type="waterfall">
            <button type="button" aria-controls="type-preview" aria-pressed="false">
