  <!-- TRUST — the four finalize gates beside a replay of a real run (output and receipt values are verbatim) -->
  <section id="trust">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head fade-up">
        <p class="section-label"><span>04</span><span data-i18n="label-trust">Verified delivery</span></p>
        <h2 class="section-heading" data-i18n="trust-h2">Checked before <em>it reaches you.</em></h2>
        <p class="section-body" data-i18n="trust-body">Finalization validates and delivers the artifact, then checks the delivered file. Diagrams also run a browser check; one-page answers run it when requested. Later check failures are reported and do not roll back the delivered file.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="trust-layout" id="trust-run">
        <ol class="gates">
          <li class="gate" style="--d:1.5s"><span class="gate-no">01</span><div><h3><code>validate</code><span data-i18n="gate-1-h">The source means what it says</span></h3><p data-i18n="gate-1-p">Schema, IDs and references, then the layout itself: crossings, label clearance, corridors and legend room. A blank chart cell is an error, not a zero.</p></div><span class="gate-pass">PASS</span></li>
          <li class="gate" style="--d:2.3s"><span class="gate-no">02</span><div><h3><code>deliver</code><span data-i18n="gate-2-h">Nothing half-written</span></h3><p data-i18n="gate-2-p">Rendered in a staging copy beside the target and swapped in atomically after delivery checks pass. A failed render does not replace the existing file.</p></div><span class="gate-pass">PASS</span></li>
          <li class="gate" style="--d:2.9s"><span class="gate-no">03</span><div><h3><code>check</code><span data-i18n="gate-3-h">The file is the one that was checked</span></h3><p data-i18n="gate-3-p">The delivered HTML is read back and checked again, and the receipt records the hashes of the source and of this exact file.</p></div><span class="gate-pass">PASS</span></li>
          <li class="gate" style="--d:3.6s"><span class="gate-no">04</span><div><h3><code>browser-check</code><span data-i18n="gate-4-h">Readable in a real browser</span></h3><p data-i18n="gate-4-p">When run, Chrome checks the artifact at several desktop sizes for overflow, text readability and controls. Browser checks are opt-in for one-page answers.</p></div><span class="gate-pass">PASS</span></li>
        </ol>
        <figure class="run">
          <div class="run-bar"><span class="window-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="run-title">finalize · cache-miss</span></div>
          <div class="run-body">
            <p class="t-line t-cmd" style="--d:0s"><span aria-hidden="true">$ </span>archify finalize sequence cache-miss.json cache-miss.html --browser-check</p>
            <p class="t-line t-ok" style="--d:3.9s">finalize pass: cache-miss.html</p>
            <p class="t-line" style="--d:4.05s">gates <b>validate:pass</b> <b>deliver:pass</b> <b>check:pass</b> <b>browser-check:pass</b></p>
            <p class="t-line" style="--d:4.2s">receipt cache-miss.finalize.json</p>
          </div>
          <div class="receipt-sum">
            <p class="sum-head" data-i18n="sum-head">From the receipt</p>
            <div class="sum-row"><span class="sum-k">check</span><span class="sum-v"><b>9/9</b><span class="chips"><i style="--d:1.6s">single_svg</i><i style="--d:1.7s">finite_svg</i><i style="--d:1.8s">orthogonal_arrows</i><i style="--d:1.9s">label_route_clearance</i><i style="--d:2s">relationship_crossings</i><i style="--d:2.1s">relationship_corridors</i><i style="--d:2.2s">container_border_runs</i><i style="--d:2.3s">route_rhythm</i><i style="--d:2.4s">legend_clearance</i></span></span></div>
            <div class="sum-row"><span class="sum-k">browser</span><span class="sum-v"><span class="chips"><i style="--d:3s">1440×900</i><i style="--d:3.15s">1600×1000</i><i style="--d:3.3s">1920×1080</i><i style="--d:3.45s">2048×1320</i></span><small data-i18n="sum-text">smallest node text 7 px · required 6 px</small></span></div>
            <div class="sum-row"><span class="sum-k">sha256</span><span class="sum-v"><code>252f687dbe79fbf9…</code></span></div>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FEATURES — one interactive centerpiece + a tight grid -->
  <section id="features">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head fade-up">
        <p class="section-label"><span>05</span><span data-i18n="label-features">Output</span></p>
        <h2 class="section-heading" data-i18n="features-h2">One file. <em>Everything inside.</em></h2>
      </header>

      <div class="features-grid">
        <figure class="feature compare fade-up">
          <div class="compare-stage" id="compare-stage" style="--split:50%">
            <img class="compare-dark" src="assets/archify-dark.png" alt="The same Archify diagram rendered in the dark theme" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <img class="compare-light" src="assets/archify-light.png" alt="Archify architecture diagram rendered in the light theme" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <span class="compare-handle" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
            <span class="compare-tag compare-tag-l" aria-hidden="true" data-i18n="cmp-light">Light</span>
            <span class="compare-tag compare-tag-r" aria-hidden="true" data-i18n="cmp-dark">Dark</span>
            <input class="compare-range" id="compare-range" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="50" aria-label="Compare light and dark theme">
          </div>
          <figcaption class="feature-body">
            <h3 data-i18n="fv1-h">Dual-theme output</h3>
            <p data-i18n="fv1-p">Every diagram ships with coordinated dark and light variable sets. The HTML theme toggle and the SVG @media prefers-color-scheme rule switch together — one file follows the reader's theme.</p>
            <span class="feature-tag" data-i18n="fv1-tag">LIGHT · DARK · ONE FILE</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="feature export fade-up d1">
          <div class="export-shot"><img src="assets/archify-menu.png" alt="Archify export menu listing PNG, JPEG, WebP, SVG, and WebM outputs" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
          <h3 data-i18n="fv2-h">One menu, every format</h3>
          <p data-i18n="fv2-p">PNG, JPEG, WebP, dual-theme SVG, WebM motion, or straight to the clipboard — every export renders natively in the browser from the same menu.</p>
          <ul class="formats" aria-label="Export formats">
            <li>PNG</li><li>JPEG</li><li>WEBP</li><li>SVG</li><li>WEBM</li><li data-i18n="exp-clip-fmt">Clipboard</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="feature cell fade-up">
          <span class="cell-glyph" aria-hidden="true">4×</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="f2-h">Ultra-crisp 4× export</h3>
          <p data-i18n="f2-p">PNG, JPEG, WebP — all rasterized natively at up to 4× source resolution by the browser. No upsampling blur. Sharp on retina displays, slides, and print.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature cell fade-up d1">
          <span class="cell-glyph" aria-hidden="true">&lt;/&gt;</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="f5-h">Self-contained HTML</h3>
          <p data-i18n="f5-p">One HTML file. Zero dependencies, no server, no runtime. Open it in any browser and it works. Share by attaching it to an email or PR comment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature cell fade-up d2">
          <span class="cell-glyph" aria-hidden="true">“ ”</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="f6-h">Iterate by chat</h3>
          <p data-i18n="f6-p">"Move the summer trip to August", "add Redis", "make the deadline red" — refine in plain words. No diagram editor to learn.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature cell fade-up d3">
          <span class="cell-glyph" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="f7-h">Inspect and play real routes</h3>
          <p data-i18n="f7-p">Route Journey keeps the complete authored path visible while you inspect any stop or play one finite, reader-controlled pass over each exact incoming relationship.</p>
          <span class="feature-tag" data-i18n="f7-tag">INSPECT · PLAY · PAUSE</span>
        </div>
        <div class="feature cell fade-up">
          <span class="cell-glyph" aria-hidden="true">[1]</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="f8-h">Sources pinned to a commit</h3>
          <p data-i18n="f8-p">Diagram nodes and page claims can point at their sources. Repository links are pinned to a full commit on GitHub or GitLab, and a page quotes the code in a source card.</p>
          <span class="feature-tag" data-i18n="f8-tag">GITHUB · GITLAB · PINNED</span>
        </div>
        <div class="feature cell fade-up d1">
          <span class="cell-glyph" aria-hidden="true">?</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="f9-h">Follow up on one panel</h3>
          <p data-i18n="f9-p">Ask about any panel, or a passage you select, and copy a message that names it. Your agent revises that panel and leaves the rest of the page untouched.</p>
          <span class="feature-tag" data-i18n="f9-tag">ASK · COPY · PATCH</span>
        </div>
        <div class="feature cell fade-up d2">
          <span class="cell-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◐</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="f10-h">Live by default</h3>
          <p data-i18n="f10-p">Each diagram type moves in a way that matches how it reads. Readers can switch to Still; motion never changes the layout or the exported geometry.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature cell fade-up">
          <span class="cell-glyph" aria-hidden="true">文A</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="f11-h">Speaks your language</h3>
          <p data-i18n="f11-p">Viewer controls ship in English, 简体中文, 繁體中文, Español and 한국어. Any other language can be supplied as data with <code>meta.translations</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature cell fade-up d1">
          <span class="cell-glyph" aria-hidden="true">Δ</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="f13-h">See what changed</h3>
          <p data-i18n="f13-p"><code>archify compare</code> draws an architecture's before and after as one delta diagram — added, removed and rerouted relationships — with a machine-readable receipt.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

